971	+`entire review --models` lists the models each review-runner agent advertises via the optional `agent.ModelLister` capability (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/model_lister.go`). claude-code returns a curated list of real aliases (opus/sonnet/haiku); Pi enumerates live by shelling out to `pi --list-models`. Agents whose CLI has no enumeration command (codex, gemini) do not implement `ListModels`, so the picker offers only Default + Custom. The `--model` flag still forwards any value the agent CLI accepts.
972	+
973	+The profile-level `task` is the shared work item. Each `agents` map entry is a worker id. For simple entries the worker id is also the agent name; to run the same agent more than once, use aliases and set `agent` plus `model`. Per-worker `skills`, `prompt`, and `model` adapt that task to agent-specific mechanics. Pi is a prompt/model-driven worker (`pi --mode json --print [--model ...]`) rather than a slash-command worker. Settings fields: `EntireSettings.ReviewProfiles` and `EntireSettings.ReviewDefaultProfile` in `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`. The old top-level `review` map is parse-tolerated and can be exposed as a legacy `general` profile when no `review_profiles` are configured.
974	+
975	 ## Behavior
976	 
977	 - Reviewers run the profile task.
978	 - Multi-reviewer profiles run reviewers concurrently, then run one judge.
979	 - Results are printed and saved locally; `output: "trail"` also posts findings to the branch trail.
980	 - A bare non-interactive `entire review` does not auto-run a profile. Automation should pass a profile name.
981	+- Profile selection is positional/`--profile` → `review_default_profile` → `general` → the only configured profile.
982	+
983	+## Flow
984	+
985	+1. `entire review` selects a profile. If no profiles exist, it runs guided setup in an interactive terminal or writes an opinionated clone-local default profile in non-interactive mode.
986	+2. It composes worker prompts via `review.ComposeReviewPrompt` and computes scope (mainline base ref via `review.ComputeScopeStats`, overridable with `--base`).
987	+3. Adapter-backed review workers (claude-code, codex, gemini-cli, pi) are spawned with `ENTIRE_REVIEW_{SESSION,AGENT,SKILLS,PROMPT,STARTING_SHA}` env vars. Their lifecycle hooks use those values to tag sessions as `Kind = "agent_review"`.
988	+4. Each spawned process has its own env, so multiple worktrees and multi-agent runs do not need a shared marker file.
989	+5. In multi-worker profiles, the configured judge receives all worker reports and produces one final verdict. The judge prompt asks it to reject unsupported claims, resolve contradictions, merge duplicates, and prioritize evidence-backed findings.
990	+6. On the next `git commit`, the PostCommit hook condenses worker review sessions into the checkpoint on `entire/checkpoints/v1`, with `Kind`, `ReviewSkills`, and `ReviewPrompt` recorded in `CommittedMetadata`.
991	+7. `CheckpointSummary.HasReview` is set for O(1) lookup. `entire status` and the re-run guard read this flag from checkpoint metadata.
992	+
993	+## Checkpoint Metadata
994	+
995	+Review metadata is stored at two levels on `entire/checkpoints/v1`:
996	+
997	+- **`CommittedMetadata` (per-session)**: `kind: "agent_review"`, `review_skills: ["/skill1", "/skill2"]`, `review_prompt: "..."`
998	+- **`CheckpointSummary` (per-checkpoint)**: `has_review: true` (umbrella; set when any session in the checkpoint has a review-kind `Kind`)
999	+
1000	+## Architecture
1001	+
1002	+- **`AgentReviewer` interface** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go`): per-agent contract with `Name() string` and `Start(ctx, RunConfig) (Process, error)`. Each adapter-backed review worker implements this in its own package.
1003	+- **`ReviewerTemplate`** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go`): shared scaffolding (spawn → pipe stdout → run parser → forward events → close). Each agent supplies only its `BuildCmd` and `Parser`.
1004	+- **`Sink` interface** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/types/sink.go`): consumers of the event stream. Production sinks include `DumpSink`, `TUISink`, and `SynthesisSink`.
1005	+- **`Run(ctx, reviewer, cfg, sinks)`** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/run.go`): single-agent orchestrator. Forwards events to sinks and calls `RunFinished` once with a populated `RunSummary`.
1006	+- **`RunMulti(ctx, reviewers, cfg, sinks)`** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/run_multi.go`): N-agent orchestrator. Agents run concurrently; events fan into a single dispatch loop so sink dispatch remains serialized.
1007	+- **Env-var contract** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/env.go`): single source of truth for `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` constants used by spawn-side and lifecycle adoption.
1008	+- **Scope detection** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/scope.go`): `detectScopeBaseRef` returns the first existing ref from `origin/HEAD → origin/main → origin/master → main → master`.
1009	+
1010	+## Multi-Agent UI
1011	+
1012	+When `RunMulti` is dispatched in a TTY, sink composition includes a live Bubble Tea dashboard plus buffered narrative/final-report output:
1013	+
1014	+- **`TUISink` / `reviewTUIModel`** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_sink.go`, `tui_model.go`, `tui_detail.go`): one row per agent with status, tokens, last assistant preview, and duration. `Ctrl+O` enters drill-in mode; `Esc` returns; `Ctrl+C` cancels through the shared context.
1015	+- **`SynthesisSink`** (`cmd/entire/cli/review/synthesis_sink.go`): in profile-native mode, runs automatically after the dump, composes an adjudication prompt covering worker narratives + per-run user prompt + profile task, calls the judge agent, and prints the final report.
1016	+- **Sink composition** (`composeMultiAgentSinks` in `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go`): pure helper taking explicit `isTTY`/`canPrompt` so tests do not depend on real TTY detection.
1017	+
1018	+## Skill Discovery (Claude Code)
1019	+
1020	+`DiscoverReviewSkills` (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/discovery.go`) walks three roots: plugin cache (`~/.claude/plugins/cache/<market>/<plugin>/<version>/{skills,commands,agents}`), user skills (`~/.claude/skills`), and user commands/agents (`~/.claude/commands`, `~/.claude/agents`).
1021	+
1022	+For the plugin cache, `pickLatestVersion` picks one version directory per plugin: highest valid semver wins; if no entries parse as semver, the lexicographic max is picked.
1023	+
1024	+## Anti-Features (do NOT recreate)
1025	+
1026	+The redesign eliminated several constructs from the prior implementation. None should be reintroduced without explicit design:
1027	+
1028	+- `PendingReviewMarker` for adapter-backed review workers (env-var handshake makes it unnecessary)
1029	+- `WorktreePath` field + worktree-scoping logic (env per process eliminates the multi-tenant problem)
1030	+- `AgentEntries` map on the marker (each agent has its own env)
1031	+- Marker overwrite tripwire / refuse-attach guard (the bug classes they defended against do not exist)
1032	+- `--track-only` flag
1033	+- `--postreview` / `--finalize` / empty review commits / `/entire-review:finish` skill installer
1034	+- `Launcher` + `HeadlessLauncher` as separate interfaces (single `AgentReviewer`)
1035	+- Codex chrome-line filtering or any agent-specific stdout post-processing in shared multi-agent code (per-agent parsers own their format)
1036	+- `sync.Once`-guarded onCancel + parallel `signal.Notify` goroutine (single cancel from start)
